          "explanation": "The oak seemed indestructible until lightning split it and revealed it had been hollow for years. It foreshadows the novel's society: impressive on the surface, but its moral and productive core has been eaten away, so it only takes a shock to expose the emptiness. The first option reverses the image's meaning. Rand celebrates industry rather than nature's revenge on it, and Eddie is famously loyal, not plotting to leave.",
