          "explanation": "Nozick was sympathetic to free markets -- his 1974 book defends a minimal state. His essay instead examined the structure of Rand's ethical argument and found gaps: it was unclear why life as a standard of value implies each person's own life is his ultimate value, or why rational self-interest rules out exploiting others. That is why it remains the standard academic critique: it attacks the reasoning, not the conclusions.",
